{"success": true, "name": "arc-task-delta-inference", "file": "references/compact-output-reassessment-after-errors.md", "content": "# Compact-output reassessment after incorrect submissions

When inputs are partitioned by repeated separator rows or columns but demos produce much smaller outputs, dimension ratios help identify possible structure but do not establish the encoding. Keep distinct hypotheses for (a) summarizing interior regions, (b) recording separator/boundary markers at their intersections, and (c) selecting only rows or columns with special markers. For each demo, write down the exact partition counts and map candidate input coordinates or blocks to each output cell, including ordering. Reproduce every output exactly before transferring the map.

After an incorrect compact-output submission, do not merely alter colors or copy another visually salient set of markers. Reopen the task class and output representation, and re-derive dimensions and correspondence from all demos. Repeated, heterogeneous demos may share only an abstract structure; spend another demo only when two explicit mappings predict a materially different discriminating observation.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1792484434/attempts/a51726d22484491ca3bb302d2d403d60/system/state/hermes/skills/puzzle-solving/arc-task-delta-inference/references/compact-output-reassessment-after-errors.md"}

{"success": true, "name": "arc-demo-evidence-recovery", "file": "references/task-29b1b5eb-instance-review.md", "content": "# Task 29b1b5eb: fresh-instance evidence caution

This review involved a new stream instance bearing a task ID that had appeared in historical skill references. The prior note suggested rightward extensions but explicitly warned it was not a validated universal rule. Transferring that hypothesis directly led to unvalidated output; repeated requests were made without an explicit discriminator or a cumulative pair-by-pair delta ledger. The resulting grid submission was reported as an invalid ARC grid, and the attempted retry repeated the same malformed shape.

A fresh task instance requires independent evidence. Treat same-ID references as historical warnings, not transformation rules. For every returned pair, immediately record exact changed coordinates and unaffected candidates, update named hypotheses, and request again only for an observation that separates plausible rules. When invalid-grid feedback arrives, check row count, widths, dimensions, values, and action serialization before making another attempt; keep format diagnosis separate from inference. This session did not establish a reliable transformation for its test, so this reference documents process failures and recovery gates, not a solved output rule.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1792484434/attempts/a51726d22484491ca3bb302d2d403d60/system/state/hermes/skills/puzzle-solving/arc-demo-evidence-recovery/references/task-29b1b5eb-instance-review.md"}
